course: dictionary
lesson: 6024
title: Meek: quiet and gentle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Meek means quiet, gentle and patient. A meek person is not easily angry and does not like to argue. Think of meek as calm and soft-spoken, not loud or pushy.
explain: Be careful, because meek can also be a warning word. When someone is too quiet and does whatever others say, meek is used with disapproval, as in «meek and timid». The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Look at the clues around it. In «when Toad is quiet and meek, playing the good little hero of a Sunday-school prize book, that's when he is at his trickiest», the words warns and trickiest show that meek is not a compliment here. Toad only looks meek; he is planning something sneaky.
explain: Use the swap check: put a word like «gentle and quiet» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning. «Meekly obey» means to obey quietly, without arguing.
fact: Meek means quiet, gentle and patient, and not easily angry.
fact: «Meek and mild» is a common pair of words that go together.
fact: «Meekly» is the adverb, so «meekly obey» means to do as you are told quietly, without arguing.
fact: Meek can mean too quiet and ready to give in, so always check the context.
fact: In the Bible, Jesus said «Blessed are the meek, for they shall inherit the earth»; Christians see meekness as gentle strength, not weakness.
exercise: «The meek little puppy let the big dog take its bone.» What does meek mean here? | *Quiet and gentle, not wanting to argue | Brave enough to fight back | Clever at hiding things | Very loud and angry
exercise: Which phrase means to do what you are told quietly, without arguing? | Wildly dance | Proudly refuse | *Meekly obey | Loudly argue back
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means quiet and gentle: «The shy girl was meek and mild in class.» | shy | *meek | girl | class
test: The Badger says Toad is «meek and mild», but Toad is up to tricks. What does meek suggest about Toad here? | *Toad is only pretending to be quiet and gentle | Toad is cheerful and funny | Toad is truly brave and loud | Toad is sleepy after a long walk
test: Which word is closest in meaning to meek? | Noisy | Bossy | *Gentle | Rude
exam: In a story, which description shows a meek character? | The cat chased the ball across the garden | The girl shouted at everyone and refused to share | The man laughed loudly at his own jokes | *The boy spoke softly and did not argue when he was teased
